    html: [https://arxiv.org/html/2109.09393](https://arxiv.org/html/2109.09393)
    abs: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.09393](https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.09393)
    pdf: [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2109.09393](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2109.09393)
\- paper\_id \`1606.07965\` — Summarizing Decisions in Spoken Meetings (Lu Wang, Claire Cardie; 2011)
    html: [https://arxiv.org/html/1606.07965](https://arxiv.org/html/1606.07965)
    abs: [https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.07965](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.07965)
    pdf: [https://arxiv.org/pdf/1606.07965](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1606.07965)
\- paper\_id \`2104.05919\` — Document-Level Event Argument Extraction by Conditional Generation (Sha Li, Heng Ji, Jiawei Han; 2021)
    html: [https://arxiv.org/html/2104.05919](https://arxiv.org/html/2104.05919)
    abs: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.05919](https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.05919)
    pdf: [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2104.05919](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2104.05919)

Analysis object (every field required unless noted):
\- paper\_id: exactly as listed above
\- title
\- research\_question: one sentence
\- methodology: 2-5 sentences
\- key\_findings: 3-8 items {finding, evidence\_type, section} where evidence\_type is
  supported, unsupported, or contradicted
\- limitations: list of strings
\- reproducibility: {code\_available, dataset\_available, metrics\_reported} booleans
\- confidence\_scores: map short finding label -> float in [0, 1]
\- raw\_claims: 5-15 short one-sentence claims, in your words if verbatim is not possible
\- source\_url: the URL you actually read
\- access: "full\_text" or "abstract\_only"

